A father describes his son, three and almost four, responding to a playful hug and declaration of love by saying he does not love daddy and wants mommy. He says he is hypersensitive, struggles with depression and cried alone, then seeks advice on regulating his response without becoming resentful. He thanks commenters for support and begins describing the words as a child still learning to communicate.

- "I was having fun with my kid after daycare yesterday. We're generally a really affectionate family, so when we were playing I came up behind my little guy, gave him a big bear hug and said "I love you buddy" to which he responded "I don't love you daddy, I want mommy"." [ar037-0038]
