- "He kicked me in my gut before and I had a miscarriage. So this age is hard. I guess what I'm wondering is, if you were absent from your child's life for the first years, were you still able to have a good relationship with them when they grew up?" [ar021-0122]
- "I think you’re right- this is definitely reinforcing some insecurities I have about choosing to go to medical school and work these long hours as a mom. You tell yourself that it’s okay and you can still be a good mom while having a career, but when my daughter rejects me it opens up more worries about whether I made the right choice." [ar069-0235]
- "We just found out I'm pregnant with #2 and I can't help but feel like this is just going to be another baby I carry who loves dad more and puts up with me.  I just feel so unwanted and left out." [ar069-0234]

**But:** The medical resident questions whether hours alone explain it: "It could be more due to that than the hours because of medical training… at least I hope" [ar069-0237]

