Status is one of: active, parked (researched, not pursued now), dropped (with the reason
in the avatar file), research only (a market-wide research folder, not a buyer).

The niche name is used unchanged in three places: `library/avatars/<niche>/`,
`~/GitHub/_research/<niche>/`, and this table. It does not change once research is
filed under it. A new understanding of the buyer gets a new niche.

## Definitions

A niche is chosen by the owner from a map of a crowd (`playbooks/new-niche.md`, "The five
steps of research"). Its definition is then one line, the subject and its range, with the counts
behind it. It never says who she is or what her problem is: the deep reading finds the
problem and the avatar says who she is. Before a map exists there is no niche to define,
only a crowd to read. Every deep-reading brief copies the definition word for word, and
`~/GitHub/_research/_tools/check_definition.py` refuses a brief that does not, or a
definition the owner has not confirmed.

### `baby-development`

- **Subject:** The development of a child from birth to 48 months.
- **Confirmed by the owner:** 2026-11-20. The owner set the range ("we are targeting 0 to 48 months"); it was not chosen from a map. Posts about older children are still recorded, as "near", so the counts can show what lies beyond 48 months.

History: until 2026-11-20 the readings stopped at 24 months, a limit carried over from an
older brief without asking the owner.
# baby-development

Research on mothers of babies 0 to 24 months who want to know what to do with the baby at
this age and whether the baby is on track. Collected October to November 2026 for the
mamiVio baby-development funnel. A new round began 2026-11-18; `brief.md` describes it and
names no product. The October brief is `_work/2026-10/brief.md`.

**Where the October round is now:** `quotes/2026-10/`, `evidence/2026-10/`,
`findings/2026-10/` (both findings pages and `her-words.md`) and `_work/2026-10/` (reading
ledgers, the Reddit selection). Wherever this page says `quotes/`, `evidence/`, `findings/`,
`her-words.md`, `_work/reddit-selection/` or `_work/reading-ledgers/` below, read it with
`2026-10/` added. The new round's working files are in `_work/2026-11/`.
Rules for all research: `../README.md`.

## The round of November 2026: where it stands (2026-11-20)

How it was run, step by step: `../_tools/README.md`.

| Step | State |
|---|---|
| Random sample of 20,000 posts read and sorted | Done for birth to 48 months (2026-11-20): 3,811 on the niche, 8,476 near, 7,713 off. `evidence/2026-11/birth-to-48-months/counts.md`. The first pass stopped at 24 months by mistake (2,471 on the niche); 12,534 posts were read again |
| Digests of each pattern | Done for birth to 24 months only: 20, in `evidence/2026-11/second-reading/` |
| Findings sections, one per pattern | Done for birth to 24 months only, not reviewed: `findings/2026-11/patterns/` |
| Findings page and her words | Written 2026-11-20 for birth to 24 months only, not reviewed: `findings/what-hurts-and-what-she-wants.md` (163 findings), `her-words.md` (247 phrases). The spec files the page was built from: `_work/2026-11/findings-build/` |
| Avatar | Not written |
| Still unread | 97,521 posts (10 April to 24 October), and all replies by people other than the poster (4.19 million downloaded, on disk only) |

## Not usable for conclusions (marked 2026-11-18)

The Reddit posts read for this niche were chosen by a word list we wrote ourselves
(`_tools/history/shared/niche_filter.py`), and posts that mention buying, paid tools or
brands were ranked first. Posts that describe the problem in other words were never seen.

- **Still good:** the download. It is complete and has no keyword in it
  (`../new-and-expecting-mothers/reddit/raw/reddit-2026/`), so nothing needs downloading
  again. The quotes are real and checked word for word, so they can be used as her words.
- **Not to be used:** the counts, the evidence file, and anything that says what is common
  or central for her.
- **What happens next:** the selection and reading are redone by the method being proven on
  `baby-development` (random sample of everything first, word list from her words after).
  Whether and when this niche is redone is the owner's decision.

For this niche in detail: the brief named a candidate product, only about 1,785 of
24,326 matched posts were read (the top-ranked group's last two months, then all posts
first set aside for hard subjects), and the two findings pages and `her-words.md` rest on
that reading. They are superseded and stay unreviewed.

